Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "FallingObjectOnRoadAtNight" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :EvidenceBasedAnomaly ;
    :hasObstacle :obstacle1 ;
    :hasEvidence :evidence1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1, :risk2 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 .

:obstacle1 a :RoadObject ;
    :description "Falling object on road surface" .

:evidence1 a :FallingObjectIndicator ;
    :description "Object appears to be falling or lying on the road" ;
    :indicatesPotentialRisk :risk1 .

:risk1 a :CollisionRisk ;
    :description "Potential collision risk due to falling object on road" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:risk2 a :OcclusionRisk ;
    :description "Risk of occlusion due to object obstructing view of road ahead" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .

:weather1 a :NightCondition ;
    :description "Scene captured during nighttime" .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.9"^^xsd:float .

:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.75"^^xsd:float .
```

Identified Risks for each risk class:

Risk 1:
Description: Potential collision risk due to falling object on road
Severity Score: 0.9

Risk 2:
Description: Risk of occlusion due to object obstructing view of road ahead
Severity Score: 0.75